id: question-packets/polanyi
title: "Polanyi axes: seven questions about what can be said"
kind: question-packet
record_shape: header
status: draft
version: 0.1.0-draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-13; the seven axes and their marks are Dave's design for the /polanyi surface, restated; each seal is the agent's prediction of Dave's mark from the records cited, sealed before the surface exists"
updated: 2026-09-13
loop_ref: core/articulation-floor.yawn
runtime_surface: https://yawn.bot/polanyi
floor_surface: https://yawn.bot/status
seal_schema_ref: schemas/articulation-floor.v0.1.schema.json

purpose: >
  Project Michael Polanyi's account of tacit knowing into seven questions a
  person can mark, so that the same card that asks any other question can ask
  these and the page measures itself. Each axis is a question. It goes through
  the four beats of core/articulation-floor.yawn: the bot's prediction of the
  reader's mark is sealed here, the reader marks, the seal is revealed and
  scored, and the reader scores the sealed reason. The two axes Polanyi never
  took a position on, timing and fidelity, are where the extension lives if it
  lives anywhere.

projection_rule: >
  These are not seven storage fields. A surface may ask them in any order,
  wording, or medium while question_key stays stable. Skipped marks become
  lacunae. The reader's mark is an answer record, never a field in this shared
  packet: you stays null here and is filled per principal by their own answer
  records, which live where core/articulation-floor.yawn says they may.

marks_rule: >
  polanyi is Polanyi's own position as reported by the sources below, on the
  same scale the reader marks. contested_by names who argued against it;
  contest_note says the argument in one line. Neither is a claim about the
  reader. Polanyi's mark is shown as content because it is the question; the
  seal is not shown until the reader has marked.

seal_rule: >
  Every axis carries one seal: the bot's prediction of the reader's mark and
  the reason it expects that mark, read from the records in source_refs on the
  reader's behalf, timestamped and hashed with lib/articulation-floor-v0.1.mjs
  before any surface rendered the question. A surface hides the seal until the
  mark is made (blind: true); this public record does not hide it, because
  what the hash protects is the bot's inability to change its guess after the
  answer, not the reader's ability to look. A reader who looks first has
  anchored their mark and should say so. scripts/validate-articulation-floor-v0.1.mjs
  recomputes every hash and fails if any axis has no seal: no seal, no question.

answer_contract_ref: question-packets/orientation-nine.yawn#answer_contract
answer_record_ref: templates/answer.yawn
floor_record_ref: records/articulation-floor.yawn

questions:
  - question_key: floor
    default_display_order: 1
    default_prompt: "Can what you know be fully said?"
    polanyi: "no"
    contested_by: [collins]
    contest_note: "relational tacit knowledge can be made explicit"
    candidates: ["no", "partly", "yes"]
    maps_to: [lacuna, proof]
    you: null
    seal:
      question: "question-packets/polanyi.yawn#floor"
      axis: floor
      predicted_answer: "partly"
      predicted_reason: "Dave's own closing line splits the mechanical, carried by intelligence, from the meaningful, carried by humans, and HOLDOUT.md measured his stated judgments predicting his revealed ones at precision 0.297; the records already commit to a remainder that cannot be said."
      confidence: 0.6
      model: "agent-on-behalf (Claude Code session, 2026-09-13) reading the records in source_refs on Dave's behalf; a prediction of Dave's mark, not Dave's mark; no provider call"
      t_sealed: "2026-09-13T05:40:00Z"
      blind: true
      source_refs: [index.html, HOLDOUT.md, JUDGMENTS.md]
      hash: sha256:736b8f463245067130604f6dcfd166b6e25287658e972a548366f1c50b475f23

  - question_key: exclusivity
    default_display_order: 2
    default_prompt: "Can you attend to a thing and through it at once?"
    polanyi: "never"
    contested_by: []
    candidates: ["never", "sometimes", "always"]
    maps_to: [scope, perspective]
    you: null
    seal:
      question: "question-packets/polanyi.yawn#exclusivity"
      axis: exclusivity
      predicted_answer: "sometimes"
      predicted_reason: "The aperture contract lets one record be looked at through several lenses without changing it, and the compute press on a question row opens what is missing from a question while it is being asked; the records treat attending to and through as switchable, not exclusive."
      confidence: 0.5
      model: "agent-on-behalf (Claude Code session, 2026-09-13) reading the records in source_refs on Dave's behalf; a prediction of Dave's mark, not Dave's mark; no provider call"
      t_sealed: "2026-09-13T05:40:00Z"
      blind: true
      source_refs: [core/projection-and-aperture.yawn, records/inquiry-aperture-one-question-face.yawn]
      hash: sha256:361740c3161fdd92b59c52c0b2318085d29f938935a8844365006a918217c4f1

  - question_key: reversibility
    default_display_order: 3
    default_prompt: "After you break a skill apart, can you put it back?"
    polanyi: "usually"
    contested_by: [tsoukas]
    contest_note: "not back to not-knowing"
    candidates: ["rarely", "usually", "always"]
    maps_to: [movement, proof]
    you: null
    seal:
      question: "question-packets/polanyi.yawn#reversibility"
      axis: reversibility
      predicted_answer: "usually"
      predicted_reason: "Every structural change in the protocol carries a source-preserving receipt so the prior state can be rebuilt, yet the migration record says the numbered generation was absorbed, not restored; the records expect to put a thing back, never back to before it was known."
      confidence: 0.55
      model: "agent-on-behalf (Claude Code session, 2026-09-13) reading the records in source_refs on Dave's behalf; a prediction of Dave's mark, not Dave's mark; no provider call"
      t_sealed: "2026-09-13T05:40:00Z"
      blind: true
      source_refs: [migrations/2026-08-17-canonical-extension.yawn, templates/structural-change-receipt.yawn]
      hash: sha256:28f7c2297b6b8a79035ab84089edf21f01f1e25240b3215edfd7903d88886dcc

  - question_key: timing
    default_display_order: 4
    default_prompt: "Does saying what you know have to happen while you're using it?"
    polanyi: "assumed yes"
    contested_by: []
    contest_note: "Polanyi never considered the after-the-fact case"
    candidates: ["yes", "sometimes", "no"]
    maps_to: [proof, movement]
    you: null
    seal:
      question: "question-packets/polanyi.yawn#timing"
      axis: timing
      predicted_answer: "no"
      predicted_reason: "The turn-close packet, the session reflection and the De-Yawn brief all articulate a move after it was made; the records are built on saying it afterwards."
      confidence: 0.7
      model: "agent-on-behalf (Claude Code session, 2026-09-13) reading the records in source_refs on Dave's behalf; a prediction of Dave's mark, not Dave's mark; no provider call"
      t_sealed: "2026-09-13T05:40:00Z"
      blind: true
      source_refs: [question-packets/turn-close.yawn, core/movement-loop.yawn]
      hash: sha256:aba1f4959b2d4fb68f7c23697a0696586a8c77d48cd9b321b8e24dbfd1aca5bc

  - question_key: fidelity
    default_display_order: 5
    default_prompt: "Is the reason you give the reason that moved you?"
    polanyi: "silent"
    contested_by: [nisbett_wilson]
    contest_note: "Telling More Than We Can Know (1977), Polanyi's line inverted"
    candidates: ["rarely", "sometimes", "usually"]
    maps_to: [proof, current-state]
    you: null
    seal:
      question: "question-packets/polanyi.yawn#fidelity"
      axis: fidelity
      predicted_answer: "sometimes"
      predicted_reason: "The proof contract says a move cannot judge itself and the judgment inventory keeps a stated reason separate from what the artifact reveals; the records expect the given reason to sometimes be the moving one and never assume it."
      confidence: 0.55
      model: "agent-on-behalf (Claude Code session, 2026-09-13) reading the records in source_refs on Dave's behalf; a prediction of Dave's mark, not Dave's mark; no provider call"
      t_sealed: "2026-09-13T05:40:00Z"
      blind: true
      source_refs: [core/proof-and-boundary.yawn, JUDGMENTS.md]
      hash: sha256:2648b0669f623a578c919c3c7945d0030c8bdc9998d6f2dace39ad7d31805435

  - question_key: locus
    default_display_order: 6
    default_prompt: "Is knowing something you do, or something that's simply true?"
    polanyi: "personal"
    contested_by: []
    candidates: ["something you do", "simply true", "both"]
    maps_to: [perspective, intent]
    you: null
    seal:
      question: "question-packets/polanyi.yawn#locus"
      axis: locus
      predicted_answer: "something you do"
      predicted_reason: "Observation is the first deliberate move in the orientation contract and a Yawn is bound to a principal, so knowing is recorded as an act by someone; the empirical half of the proof contract keeps claims answerable to evidence without making them impersonal."
      confidence: 0.6
      model: "agent-on-behalf (Claude Code session, 2026-09-13) reading the records in source_refs on Dave's behalf; a prediction of Dave's mark, not Dave's mark; no provider call"
      t_sealed: "2026-09-13T05:40:00Z"
      blind: true
      source_refs: [core/orientation.yawn, core/proof-and-boundary.yawn, agents/yawn.bot.yawn]
      hash: sha256:db6d373c1a6f112930248d9182d246831400a128d3c2ad9874be41f0ca99e3c5

  - question_key: levels
    default_display_order: 7
    default_prompt: "Can a whole be read off from its parts?"
    polanyi: "no"
    contested_by: []
    contest_note: "boundary conditions harness the lower level; holonic"
    candidates: ["no", "partly", "yes"]
    maps_to: [placement, boundary]
    you: null
    seal:
      question: "question-packets/polanyi.yawn#levels"
      axis: levels
      predicted_answer: "no"
      predicted_reason: "The holarchy contract lets a child inherit selected context but never truth, consent, privacy, proof or authority; the whole is not the sum of what the parts carry."
      confidence: 0.75
      model: "agent-on-behalf (Claude Code session, 2026-09-13) reading the records in source_refs on Dave's behalf; a prediction of Dave's mark, not Dave's mark; no provider call"
      t_sealed: "2026-09-13T05:40:00Z"
      blind: true
      source_refs: [core/holarchy.yawn, index.html]
      hash: sha256:05c5573fcc9818f5bd2510fe0fe50a550c52419cf5747616f0b00f8ce2cd33fc

readout_ref: core/articulation-floor.yawn#readout

sources:
  - text: "Michael Polanyi, Personal Knowledge (1958) and The Tacit Dimension (1966): we can know more than we can tell; subsidiary and focal awareness; tacit knowing as personal; boundary conditions harnessing a lower level."
    epistemic_status: reported
  - text: "Harry Collins, Tacit and Explicit Knowledge (2010): relational tacit knowledge could in principle be made explicit; somatic and collective tacit knowledge resist it differently."
    epistemic_status: reported
  - text: "Haridimos Tsoukas, Do we really understand tacit knowledge? (2003): tacit knowledge is not converted into explicit knowledge; articulation displays it in a new context without abolishing the tacit."
    epistemic_status: reported
  - text: "Richard Nisbett and Timothy Wilson, Telling More Than We Can Know (1977): verbal reports on mental processes are often confabulated; the reason given is not reliably the reason that moved."
    epistemic_status: reported
  - text: "Dave, 2026-09-13, the /polanyi design (surface, records, loop): the seven axes, Polanyi's marks, the contests, and the four beats, recorded on his behalf."
    epistemic_status: reported

boundaries:
  - "A mark is the reader's; the seal is the bot's; neither is a diagnosis."
  - "Seven of seven marked does not mean true, and a hit does not mean the bot understood."
  - "Polanyi's mark is content, not a recommendation; the scale is a projection, not a measurement of the reader's worth."
  - "A seal that was seen before the mark is anchored; a floor built from anchored seals measures agreement, not prediction."
  - "The packet holds no answer; where answers persist is an open question in questions/open-questions.yawn."

links:
  - core/articulation-floor.yawn
  - schemas/articulation-floor.v0.1.schema.json
  - templates/seal.yawn
  - templates/answer.yawn
  - templates/floor.yawn
